60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"We have a Microbiome Atlas, Protein Folding, Amphibian Regeneration, and Plant Drought Signaling.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Sakura,,No to Plant Drought! The glasshouses are booked solid.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,The Microbiome Atlas is a catalogue project. Those are the ones that keep providing value.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Protein Folding needs spectroscopy, right? That suite is a disaster. I vote against B.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Amphibian Regeneration needs the animal facility. It's accredited, but the costs are now very high.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,The Atlas needs sequences and metadata. We have plenty of people for code and modelling now.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"And the Atlas uses field sites, but maybe the repository turnaround is better now?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Servas, would the Atlas be considered a ""catalogue"" project?","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Sakura, the field sites are still risky, but the Atlas is more about the data than a single site.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"The Atlas is the most viable. No glasshouses, no expensive animal units, and it leverages the free computing.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,I agree. The technical staff for data and modelling are available in numbers.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Sakura,,It seems the Atlas is the only one that doesn't hit a wall we've discovered.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,It fits the pattern of long-term success I found in the closeout files.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"It's the safest bet. No spectroscopy, no greenhouses, no breeding colonies.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,It is the logical choice given the current infrastructure constraints.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,I am satisfied. Let us vote.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Sakura,,Me too!,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I agree.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Takumi,,Let's do it.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
